{"availability":"available","full":"rNLKJA/Unimelb-undergraduate-2021-INFO30005-Project","name":"Unimelb-undergraduate-2021-INFO30005-Project","description":"Snacks in a Van — a dual-portal (customer + vendor) food ordering web app built with Node.js, Express, MongoDB and Handlebars. University of Melbourne INFO30005 Web Information Technologies group project, 2021.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2022-03-12T09:58:01Z","updated":"2026-10-09T09:51:51Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://snacks-in-a-van.vercel.app","topics":["express","handlebars","mongodb","mongoose","nodejs","passport-js","university-of-melbourne","web-development"],"demo":"https://snacks-in-a-van.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:39.023Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:39.023Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:39.023Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T11:02:39.023Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["INFO30005 Web Information Technologies, University of Melbourne, Semester 1 2021. Group 4399 (tutorial T03). Revived in 2026 by Sunchuangyu (Rin) Huang.","Snacks in a Van is a two-portal food-ordering web app for a business of roving snack vans. It was our team's 2021 group project, originally built with Express, Handlebars and MongoDB Atlas. The database and Heroku deployment are long gone, so the app has been rebuilt as a single full-stack Next.js application with a local-first SQLite database, a key-less map and one-click demo accounts.","place or a dropped pin; Melbourne Uni by default), browse the eight-item menu, check out, then track the order live: a status timeline, a 15-minute countdown ring, a 10-minute window to change or cancel, and a one-off rating (allowed at any stage, as in 2021). A community board shows snackers' posts, recent ratings and the top-rated vans."],"features":["| Landing page. The story, the live customer/vendor demo and one-click demo accounts. | Landing page, dark mode. The same page in dark mode. | | Find a van. The five nearest open vans, ranked by the ported 2021 distance…","1. Customer orders (/customer): From the landing page to a live order: find the nearest open van, add to the cart, place the order and follow it on the tracker, including what happens when the 15-minute promise runs out.","Start on the landing page and try the customer app with the one-click demo account","Use my location: open vans are ranked by distance and the five nearest are listed","Pick the nearest van, Ardeth Lavon at the University of Melbourne"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rNLKJA/Unimelb-undergraduate-2021-INFO30005-Project/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"65de6d74c8a9c7d446da00a32139ccf8e808e6f62a074b8679eeee39df513c63","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:39.179Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:39.179Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"INFO30005 Web Information Technologies, University of Melbourne, Semester 1 2021. Group 4399 (tutorial T03). Revived in 2026 by Sunchuangyu (Rin) Huang.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rNLKJA/Unimelb-undergraduate-2021-INFO30005-Project/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Log in as the demo vendor, van Ardeth Lavon, with one click","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rNLKJA/Unimelb-undergraduate-2021-INFO30005-Project/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Vendors sign in with their van's name, set the van's location (GPS or a click on the","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rNLKJA/Unimelb-undergraduate-2021-INFO30005-Project/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"65de6d74c8a9c7d446da00a32139ccf8e808e6f62a074b8679eeee39df513c63","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/rNLKJA/Unimelb-undergraduate-2021-INFO30005-Project/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:39.180Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T09:51:51Z","readmeSnapshot":{"